WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:11.009
In this video you embroider your very first design of your own: a round patch with a wave.

00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:14.560
All you need is the mouse and two minutes.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.188
Click “New” on the left.

00:00:18.188 --> 00:00:20.709
An empty design appears.

00:00:20.709 --> 00:00:28.587
The dashed frame is your hoop, here one hundred by one hundred millimetres.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.776
The drawing tools are on the left of the canvas.

00:00:33.776 --> 00:00:38.786
Take the ellipse and drag out a circle while holding Shift.

00:00:38.786 --> 00:00:45.580
As soon as you let go, it is already stitched: as a fill, suited to your fabric.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:49.568
On the right you see how big it is.

00:00:49.568 --> 00:00:53.547
Just type sixty millimetres, the height follows.

00:00:54.633 --> 00:00:59.280
A click on the colour swatch opens the threads.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.553
I'll take a light blue.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:03.851
Now the wave.

00:01:03.851 --> 00:01:09.589
With the pen, a click sets a corner and dragging makes a curve.

00:01:09.589 --> 00:01:11.775
Enter finishes the line.

00:01:11.775 --> 00:01:16.147
A line is stitched as a running stitch at first.

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:26.827
For a bold wave, set the type to satin, drag the width to three millimetres and give it white thread.

00:01:27.933 --> 00:01:36.573
The space bar shows you how the machine stitches: first the blue circle, then the wave.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:45.083
Under Display, “Realistic threads” shows your design the way it will look on the fabric.

00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:46.347
Nice, isn't it?

00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:54.708
Finally, choose your machine's format on the left and save.

00:01:54.708 --> 00:01:57.913
Your first design is done.
